---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const services = (await getCollection('services', ({ data }) => !data.draft)).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const url = `${site.url}/about/`;

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    '@id': `${url}#page`,
    name: `About ${site.name}`,
    url,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${site.url}/#website` },
    about: { '@id': `${site.url}/#organization` },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    '@id': `${url}#breadcrumbs`,
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${site.url}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: url },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About Us | ${site.name}`}
  description="Who we are: a free referral service that connects Severna Park, MD homeowners with a local roofer for roof leak repair. How it works and what we don't do."
  schema={schema}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About us"
    title="A leak-focused referral service for Severna Park homes"
    lede="We do one thing: help homeowners with a leaking roof reach a local roofing provider quickly, and explain leaks clearly enough that you know what to ask."
    crumb="About"
  />

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose" data-content>
      <h2>Why a site only about roof leaks?</h2>
      <p>
        Most roofing websites try to sell everything: new roofs, gutters, siding, windows. When your ceiling is
        dripping, that isn't much help. You need to know what's probably causing it, how urgent it is, and who can
        come and fix it. {site.name} was built around that moment. Every page on this site is about finding and
        fixing leaks in and around {site.city}, {site.stateName}, from <a href="/roof-flashing-repair/">failed
        flashing</a> to <a href="/chimney-leak-repair/">leaking chimneys</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Leaks are also the part of roofing where homeowners get the worst deal. A stain gets caulked from the inside,
        a patch goes on the wrong spot, and the water comes back with the next storm. We think the best protection
        is a clear explanation, so the guides here explain how water actually travels, how the real source is found,
        and what a lasting repair looks like.
      </p>

      <h2>How does {site.name} work?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>{site.name} is a free referral service, not a roofing contractor.</strong> We don't employ roofers,
        own trucks, carry contractor's insurance or perform repairs. When you call {site.phone.display}, your call is
        connected to an independent roofing provider who serves {site.city} and the surrounding {site.county}
        communities.
      </p>
      <p>
        That provider is a separate business. They inspect your roof, give you their price, schedule the work and
        stand behind it under their own terms. Any agreement for work is between you and the provider. We may be
        compensated by the provider for connecting calls; you are never charged by us for calling.
      </p>
      <aside class="callout callout--tip"><p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Before any work starts, ask the provider for their Maryland Home Improvement Commission (MHIC) licence number and proof of insurance, and get the scope and price in writing. These are reasonable questions for any contractor.</p></aside>

      <h2>What we promise, and what we don't</h2>
      <p>We keep our claims to things we can actually stand behind:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Calling is free and doesn't commit you to anything.</li>
        <li>The information on this site is written to be accurate and practical, and we correct it when we learn something is wrong.</li>
        <li>We don't publish invented reviews, ratings, prices or awards.</li>
        <li>We don't claim a street address or an office we don't have.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        What we can't promise: a provider's exact availability, response time or prices. Those are set by the provider,
        so ask them directly on the call. If something about a provider's work concerns you, tell us at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where do we help?</h2>
      <p>
        The focus is {site.city} (ZIP {site.zip}), with calls also taken from nearby
        <a href="/roof-leak-repair-arnold-md/">Arnold</a>, <a href="/roof-leak-repair-pasadena-md/">Pasadena</a>,
        <a href="/roof-leak-repair-millersville-md/">Millersville</a>, <a href="/roof-leak-repair-severn-md/">Severn</a>
        and <a href="/roof-leak-repair-glen-burnie-md/">Glen Burnie</a>. Each area page explains the leak patterns
        typical of its housing and setting, from wooded lots to waterfront homes and townhome rows.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is behind the site?</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is run by a small independent web publisher, not a roofing company. The site is built to be fast,
        readable on a phone in a dark attic, and useful even if you never call. If you spot something on a page that is
        wrong or unclear, or a provider didn't treat you well, email us. We read every message and update the guides
        when a reader points out a better way to explain something.
      </p>

      <h2>How the guides are written</h2>
      <p>
        The content here explains general, well-established roofing knowledge: how flashing is layered, why pipe boots
        crack, how water tracing works, what affects repair cost. Local details are limited to things that are widely
        known about the area, like its weather, its rivers and its housing. We don't quote prices, because a fair price
        depends on what's found on your roof. If you're new to roof leaks, start with the
        <a href="/">roof leak repair overview</a> and the symptom checker.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="about-services">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHead eyebrow="What we cover" title="Leak repairs explained on this site" id="about-services" />
      <div class="related">
        {
          services.map((s) => (
            <article class="card" data-reveal>
              <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name={s.data.icon as any} /></span>
              <h3><a href={`/${s.id}/`}>{s.data.title}</a></h3>
              <span class="text-link">Read the guide <Icon name="arrow" /></span>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand eyebrow="Talk to a local roofer" title="Have a leak? One call is all it takes." text="Describe what you're seeing and you'll be connected with a provider who serves Severna Park." />
</BaseLayout>
